      "writtenOn": "2021-01-27T02:03:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It might also affect USB boot.\n\nA 1 line explanation on why we need to exit mode on warm reboot in the OS : \n\nbecause if we were in TBT mode when a kernel panic occurred or reboot was invoked, then on reboot, the EC will still have the peripheral in TBT mode and subsequently, we\u0027d be in TBT mode on login screen (typecd cannot exit modes on init, because there it can crash and respawn mid user-session).",
      "parentUuid": "91a71e59_97dc159c",
